{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2131201979/4/codegen_prompts/2.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/4`\n- 题号：`2`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2131201979/4/2.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"2\">\n- `description`：将散落的彩色碎片按形状互补关系拼合，再按拼合体的面积从小到大垂直堆叠到输出网格中。\n- `Input structure`：背景为black。网格中散布着若干彩色像素块（4-连通分量），每个分量的颜色各不相同。这些分量恰好可以两两配对：同一对中的两个分量形状互补，即将其中一个平移后与另一个合并恰好形成一个无间隙的实心矩形。每对分量中两个颜色不同。\n- `Rule`：\n  1. 找到所有4-连通的彩色分量，计算每个分量的bounding box。\n  2. 将分量两两配对：两个分量的bounding box尺寸相同，且将一个分量叠加到另一个分量上后，二者像素恰好互补（填满整个bounding box，无重叠无间隙）。\n  3. 合并每对分量为一个矩形，矩形中每个像素保留其原始颜色。\n  4. 按每个拼合矩形的面积从小到大排序，将它们从上到下垂直堆叠在输出网格中，相邻矩形之间留一行背景色间隔，左对齐。\n- `Key insight`：碎片的形状本身编码了配对信息——互补形状是唯一的匹配依据；解题者需先通过视觉直觉识别哪些碎片能拼成矩形，再按面积排序堆叠，两步推理缺一不可。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/d749d46f, train/18447a8d, eval/62593bfd, eval/58490d8a, train/f0100645, train/8abad3cf, train/57edb29d, train/25c199f5\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d749d46f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4369\nmechanism=0.5795\nlexical=0.0141\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:sort_order, operation:translate, relation:aligned, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d749d46f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/d749d46f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPack each solid foreground rectangle twice: wide across the top and tall from the bottom.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has one background color and one foreground color; the foreground forms\nseparate solid rectangles, ordered from left to right.\n\nRule\nBuild a 10-row background canvas whose width is the packed width of the wide\nversions of the rectangles. For each source rectangle, paint a top-aligned\nrectangle of shape min(h,w) by max(h,w), with one background column between\nconsecutive rectangles. Then, starting again from the left edge, paint a\nbottom-aligned rectangle of shape max(h,w) by min(h,w) for each source rectangle,\nagain separated by one background column.\n\nKey insight\nThe input rectangles are not copied in their original orientations; each object\ncontributes one horizontal-facing and one vertical-facing normalized rectangle,\npreserving left-to-right object order.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"solid monochromatic foreground rectangles ordered left-to-right\",\n  \"dst\": \"packed upper wide slots and lower tall slots in the same left-to-right order\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"rank(s) == rank(d) for both the upper and lower slot sequences\",\n  \"transform\": \"paint each rectangle twice: min(h,w) by max(h,w) top-aligned in the upper band, and max(h,w) by min(h,w) bottom-aligned in the lower band, with one background column between slots\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"height 10; width is the sum of max(h,w) over source rectangles plus one separator column between consecutive rectangles\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"18447a8d\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3877\nmechanism=0.5364\nlexical=0.0146\ncode_feature=0.1667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:shape_match, operation:sort_order, operation:translate, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/18447a8d.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/18447a8d.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove each right-side colored shape into the left slot whose template color is its exact complement.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has two equal-width slots separated by one background column.\n- Non-background rows form horizontal bands separated by all-background rows.\n- Each band has a shared template color in the left slot and one colored source shape in the right slot.\n\nRule:\n- For each band, define its destination shape as the cells in the left slot not occupied by the template color.\n- Normalize every right-side source shape to right-slot coordinates and match it to the unique equal destination shape.\n- Clear the original right-side source pixels and paint the matched left-slot complement with the source color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe right-side objects are not placed by row order; each one completes the unique left template whose missing cells have the same shape.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"colored source shape s in a right slot\",\n  \"dst\": \"left-slot missing-cell complement d of the shared-color template in the same band\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"normalized shape(s) == normalized shape(d)\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear s and fill d with s.color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"62593bfd\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3889\nmechanism=0.4500\nlexical=0.0143\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:rotation, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:shape_match, operation:sort_order, operation:translate, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/62593bfd.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/62593bfd.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSort objects to top or bottom edge by whether their shape (up to rotation/flip) is shared.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Several multicolor connected components (8-connected) scattered across the grid.\n\nRule:\n- Compute each object's canonical shape (binary mask, invariant to rotation and flip).\n- Objects whose shape appears in two or more components → translate to TOP edge (row 0).\n- Objects whose shape is unique → translate to BOTTOM edge (row H−h).\n- Horizontal position (left column) is preserved; only vertical translation changes.\n\nKey insight: The sorting criterion is shape frequency (rotation-invariant), not area — duplicated shapes go up, unique shapes go down.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"all connected components (objects) on the background\",\n  \"dst\": \"translate each object d vertically to an edge (x preserved)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"group objects by their pixel-count (area). If an area value occurs >=2 times, those objects go to the TOP edge; if the area is unique, that object goes to the BOTTOM edge\",\n  \"transform\": \"duplicated-size -> top; singleton-size -> bottom\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"58490d8a\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4065\nmechanism=0.5413\nlexical=0.0208\ncode_feature=0.2857\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:sort_order, operation:translate, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/58490d8a.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/58490d8a.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nCount colored objects and record tallies inside a legend box.\n\nInput structure:\n- A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.\n- Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.\n\nRule:\n- For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.\n- Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.\n\nKey insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"colored sprites s outside the black legend bbox\",\n  \"dst\": \"follow pixels d inside the black legend bbox (one per key color)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.color == d.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"s reduces to 1 dot placed left-to-right starting at pos(d) with 1 bg pixel gap, replacing d\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"f0100645\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3443\nmechanism=0.4141\nlexical=0.0135\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:translate, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/f0100645.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/f0100645.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide each inner colored object horizontally into the same-colored vertical wall until it touches an obstacle.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- The only foreground colors are two non-background colors.\n- One foreground color fills the left column and the other fills the right column.\n- Extra 8-connected objects of each wall color appear away from that color's wall.\n\nRule\n- Clear the extra objects from their original positions.\n- For each wall color, process its 8-connected extra objects from nearest to farthest from the matching wall.\n- Slide each object horizontally toward its matching wall as far as possible without overlapping the wall or an already settled object of the same color.\n- Keep the two vertical wall columns fixed.\n\nKey insight\n- The side columns act like color-specific gravity walls: same-colored objects compact sideways against their own wall while preserving each object's shape.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"8-connected objects away from the full-height side wall of the same color\",\n  \"path\": \"horizontal slide toward the matching side wall, stopping just before the wall or an already settled same-color object would overlap\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"translate each object rigidly to its final unobstructed position\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
